<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African April trade data now due Tuesday.</title>
<headline>S.African April trade data now due Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>April trade data would now only be released on Tuesday at 1200 GMT, a Customs and Excise spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The data was originally scheduled for Monday.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast the trade balance would show a 900 million rand surplus in April from a 1.98 billion rand surplus in March.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
